-- title:
--   Corollary 5.5: separation of the lifted JM sequence
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge2$ and $p,q\ge0$ be integers. On $V^{\otimes p}\otimes V^{*\otimes q}$, $V=\mathbb C^d$, use the physical matrix-image tower $A_0\subset A_1\subset\cdots\subset A_{p+q}$ obtained by adding the primal registers first and then the dual registers. Unused factors carry identities. Let $\mathcal X_k$ be the algebra generated by the centers $Z(A_1),\ldots,Z(A_k)$, and let $J_k$ be the explicit signed swap/contraction sum of Eqs.(85),(86), with parameter $\delta=d$. For a first dual step use $J_1=dI$.
--
--   The lifted sequence is separating:
--   $$
--   J_k\in\mathcal X_k,\qquad \mathcal X_k=\langle J_1,\ldots,J_k\rangle_{\mathbb C}\qquad(1\le k\le p+q).
--   $$
--   The conclusion is algebra generation at each level, rather than only distinct spectral labels. It supplies the separation condition for the JM construction.
-- source:
--   Linear programming with unitary-equivariant constraints, arXiv:2207.05713v2, PDF p. 28, Corollary 5.5: separation of the lifted JM sequence

